Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: PDFium
Upstream-Contact: https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium
Source: https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium
Comment:
 The source package consists of this repository (Meson build definitions,
 acquisition and test tooling, Debian packaging; BSD-3-Clause, see "Files: *")
 and, as the "upstream" component, the PDFium revision pinned in
 sources.lock.json plus the files of its DEPS dependencies listed there,
 exported unmodified from their official Git repositories (googlesource.com).
 Paths below upstream/pdfium/ are PDFium's own layout.
 .
 Not exported (upstream.toml export_exclude, recorded in sources.lock.json):
 the standalone test font binaries under testing/resources/fonts/,
 testing/resources/font_tests/ and third_party/NotoSans*/, which only
 upstream's own tests use.
 .
 The binary packages contain object code from: PDFium (BSD-3-Clause, including
 its built-in Foxit fonts in core/fxge/fontdata), the Chromium build headers
 (BSD-3-Clause), AGG (AGG license), OpenJPEG (BSD-2-Clause), the FreeType
 PostScript glyph name tables (FTL), and the header-only fast_float (used
 under MIT) and dragonbox (used under BSL-1.0) libraries. No test documents or
 fonts from upstream's testing/ directory are installed. The other
 directories listed below are part of the source only and are not compiled.

